// microbench hop1_knows_out: the distinct knows-neighbors of a person, outgoing edges only (T1).
// Reads: the knows _from edge index from the anchor; returns each neighbor's _key only.
// Evaluator: queries/hop.py _hop1("knows", "out", "Person") -- read_neighbors + dedup,
// count-final (the harness counts the returned keys).
// mb2 lineage: MB21 (1-hop OUTBOUND).
FOR v IN 1..1 OUTBOUND CONCAT("Person/", @personId) knows
    OPTIONS {order: "bfs", uniqueVertices: "global"}
    RETURN v._key
